    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "止也。从宀𠈇聲。𠈇，古文夙。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "In the oracle bone script, an ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 人 (“person”) + ⿴囗⿱人仌 (“bamboo mat”) – a person resting on a mat. Sometimes a house (宀) was added.\nLater the pictogram of the bamboo mat became 㐁 or 𠀬, and eventually came to be written 百.\nContrast 寒.\n; “To stay overnight; lodge > night; mansion of the zodiac [i.e. the Sun's lodging stations]”"
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "止也。从宀𠈇聲。𠈇，古文夙。",
